.TH FREECLOUD-CLI 1 "June 2026" "FreeCloud 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
freecloud-cli \- synchronize files with a self-hosted FreeCloud drive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B freecloud-cli
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B freecloud-cli
runs the FreeCloud synchronization client in a terminal. If no saved
configuration is available, it starts the first-time setup prompts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Use the specified FreeCloud client configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-local \fIFOLDER\fR
Use the specified local synchronization folder.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run one synchronization pass and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-interval \fISECONDS\fR
Set the polling interval. The minimum is two seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-delete\-remote
Propagate local deletions to the remote server.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the FreeCloud version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display command help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/freecloud/last_config.json
Last-used configuration.
.TP
.I LOCAL_FOLDER/.freecloud_client.json
Configuration for a synchronized local folder.
.SH AUTHOR
Kyle Benzle <kbe@gmx.us>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR freecloud (1)
